From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:24:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(llama-cpp): speak with OmniVoice on llama.cpp's own
 audio generation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Carried as a llama.cpp patch beside the others
(patches/0012-mtmd-omnivoice.patch): OmniVoice (k2-fsa/OmniVoice), which
LocalAI serves today from a backend of its own (omnivoice-cpp, another ggml,
another build), becomes a model of the llama.cpp backend - a text model and
an mmproj, spoken through the TTS call this backend already answers for
Qwen3-TTS and the others. Nothing in LocalAI's own sources changes.

The patch adds the architecture `omnivoice` to libllama (the backbone: Qwen3
layers read in both directions, no KV cache), the projector type `omnivoice`
to libmtmd (the audio heads and the codec decoder) with an audio encoder
beside it for voice clips, the pipeline to mtmd-helper (the 32 decoding
steps, cloning, described voices, long texts, post-processing), and
vendors omnivoice.cpp's host-side rules unchanged (MIT). Its description
gives the detail, and the one deliberate difference from omnivoice.cpp: the
sequences are masked as the reference model masks them, where omnivoice.cpp
adds its mask to the attention scores.

STAGED: synthesis from text, from a voice clip and from a described voice
is built and gated on the CPU against omnivoice.cpp step by step
(docs/notes/omnivoice-on-our-backend.md, §7.4, §8 and §9, in the Louise
repository). The card comes before it joins the series.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
