++// OmniVoice (k2-fsa/OmniVoice): masked generative decoding, nothing is autoregressive
++// - the prompt is the text to speak, inp->lang its language (a name or a code of the model, optional)
++// - a step reads two sequences on a backbone context of its own: the conditional one (style, text, the codes of a
++//   voice, the target frames) and the unconditional one (the target frames alone); the audio heads of the mmproj
++//   turn the states of the target frames into logits, guidance combines the two
++// - 32 steps reveal the 8 codebooks of every frame, the most confident first, then the codec decodes them
++// - a voice clip (inp->speaker_ref, with its transcript in speaker_ref_text) is encoded to codec frames by the audio
++//   encoder of the mmproj and put before the target frames; without one the model picks a voice
++// - a voice can be described instead ("female, young adult, british accent"): the "tts" chat template of the text
++//   model puts the description before the text, between <|instruct_start|> and <|instruct_end|>
